          "narratives": {
            "headline": "WAF delivers a largely pre-released 4QCY25 with group production of 112koz, a stronger-than-expected Kiaka ramp-up offsetting Sanbrado softness, and group AISC of A$2,401/oz coming in 6% better than forecast.",
            "exec_summary": "West African Resources delivered a solid 4QCY25, with group gold production of 112koz coming in line with expectations as a stronger-than-anticipated Kiaka result of 62.3koz more than offset a softer Sanbrado quarter of 49.7koz, capping a full-year CY25 output of 300.3koz at the lower end of guidance. Group AISC of A$2,401/oz came in approximately 6% below prior forecasts, with Sanbrado's cost efficiency of A$2,152/oz helping to counterbalance the higher Kiaka AISC of A$2,536/oz as that asset continues through its ramp-up phase. The balance sheet strengthened materially over the quarter, with cash of A$584m and bullion on hand of A$177m representing a combined liquidity position that rose approximately 73% quarter-on-quarter, underscoring the company's growing free cash flow generation. Overall, the tone is constructive: the Kiaka ramp-up is progressing well \u2014 with recoveries improving to 92.9% and the plant now connected to stable grid power \u2014 and the analyst maintains a Buy rating with an unchanged price target of A$6.40, implying meaningful upside from current levels.",
            "production": "West African Resources delivered group production of 112koz in 4QCY25, up 21% quarter-on-quarter, with the result largely pre-released and in line with analyst estimates. Kiaka was the standout performer, contributing 62.3koz against more conservative prior forecasts, benefiting from head grades of 1.0g/t \u2014 ahead of the 0.9g/t estimate \u2014 and improved recoveries of 92.9% versus the prior quarter's 88.2%, supported by the plant's connection to stable grid power. Sanbrado came in softer than expected at 49.7koz, though its lower AISC of A$2,152/oz partially offset the production shortfall, with the two assets together delivering full-year CY25 output of 300.3koz at the lower end of guidance.",
            "outlook": "With Kiaka now connected to stable grid power and recoveries tracking above expectations at 92.9%, WAF is well-positioned to ramp toward the analyst-forecast ~455koz in CY26, with Kiaka alone expected to contribute ~245koz as the dominant production centre. Key catalysts include continued Kiaka throughput and grade delivery against the CY26 production ramp, while principal risks centre on further cost inflation at Kiaka \u2014 where AISC of A$2,536/oz remains elevated \u2014 as well as any operational disruption at Sanbrado, which underperformed in 4QCY25, and ongoing geopolitical risk inherent to the Burkina Faso operating environment."
          }
